KEPT (verified): `benchmark-board.yml` (moves, never deleted; 1008's board = 23 entries / 17 defect-bearing, test-anchored); `docs/research/ensemble-decorrelation-evidence.md`; the decorrelation rule (reworded per REIMAGINE); gaze fail-open semantics; `events.jsonl` + `permission-diffs/` — the `CLAUDE_TELEMETRY_DIR` env var itself SURVIVES (read by `bin/usage-report:16`, `bin/snapshot:6`; set by `skills/lair/log-agent-metrics`) — only the celebration seam dies; 0870/0936/0902/0990 untouched; historical scorecard log lines never deleted.
REIMAGINE: Four ordered passes. 1 Gate: verify 1005+1006+1007 merged (no recording gap); confirm 1007's PR moved `enumerate-merges.py` (+ test). 2 Celebration teardown: delete step 2 + line 25; renumber (and patch the five cross-refs) or keep numbering stable; delete `log-celebration` + `enumerate-merges.py` original + both telemetry tests; reword lair step 0 + `check-close-claims.sh` comment; optional one-time machine-local archive of `~/.claude/telemetry/celebrations.jsonl` (outside the repo). 3 Reviewers thinning: create `skills/coaching/SKILL.md` (thin REPLAY descriptor, fail-loud, cold path); move the §8 "Move" column into it; delete the "Drop" column; rewrite `reviewers/SKILL.md` to descriptor-only (needs-description + contract prose mirroring the AGENTS.md harness paragraph, live route docs, fail-open, one pointer each to `/coaching` and the project's attribution records — no subcommand table); gaze + raid rewords; `make skills-catalog`. 4 Dispositions + rule (mechanical): `erg close` 0980 WONTDO (premise "seat each runtime behind the runner" dropped by §2; cite §10); verify 0205/0356 headers (no write); exactly one annotation log line each on the seven closed trial tickets pointing at the spec §10 (scorecards stay); reword `rules/workflow.md:107-108` keeping the gradient — the rule now binds runtime-native reviewers, not sandboxed seats (it is already seat-mechanism-free; the change is gradient completion). Final: git grep sweep + `make check`.
ANTIPATTERNS: Teardown before capture lands (recording gap, §10). Deleting historical scorecard lines (annotate only). Touching `events.jsonl`/`permission-diffs/` or the shared `CLAUDE_TELEMETRY_DIR` readers. Dangling references (lair:16, `check-close-claims.sh:18-21`, raid:326/341, README catalog, renumbered-roar cross-refs, `test_benchmark_board.sh:47` if the board moves, orphaned `references/*.md` — `test_skill_reference_pointers.py` fails on both dead pointers and unpointed files). Deleting `benchmark-board.yml` or the decorrelation evidence doc. Deleting the seat-runner (it moves). Touching the forge-bot paragraph or internal-panel tests. Re-closing/editing closed 0205/0356 headers. Forgetting `make skills-catalog`. Renumbering without patching the five cross-refs.
EXIT-CRITERIA: Box 1 — reduced suite green (board test, Padmé-route test, surviving dispatcher tests); `git grep` of `skills/reviewers/` empty of roster/trial machinery; no `panel.yml`; frontmatter/reference-pointer tests pass; catalog regenerated. Box 2 — `git grep` `log-celebration` and `roar-last-sha` empty across `skills/ tests/ scripts/ bin/ rules/` (this is what forces the lair + `check-close-claims.sh` rewords); no telemetry step in roar SKILL.md; a live /roar run appends nothing. Box 3 — 0980 gains a `Closed:` WONTDO citing §10; 0205 header verified (no write); exactly one new spec-pointing log line in each of the seven trial tickets; `erg check` passes. Box 4 — integration-review check at close (records are project-local; the harness PR cannot assert it): enumerate merges since 1005's merge SHA, each reviewed merge has a §4 record naming its reviewers; a reviewed PR without one is a §4.8 fail-loud defect. Verdict: keep-as-is (blind spots absorbed by the existing grep-clean criteria and §8/§10 — no reword needed).

